NAME
       fold - wrap long lines to a given width

SYNOPSIS
       fold [-w WIDTH] [-s] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
       fold breaks every line of FILE (or standard input) that is longer than
       WIDTH characters (80 by default) into several lines.

OPTIONS
       -w WIDTH, --width=WIDTH
              The maximum line length.

       -s, --spaces
              Break at spaces where possible, so words stay whole.

EXAMPLES
           fold -s -w 60 /root/notes.txt

SEE ALSO
       fmt(1), cut(1)
